---
import Sheet from "../layouts/Sheet.astro";
import bundle from "../data/bundle.json";

const live = bundle.companies.filter((c) => !c.missing);
const dropped = live.reduce((n, c) => n + (c.results.reconciliation?.dropped ?? []).length, 0);
const pill = { text: dropped ? `${dropped} lens drops` : "no lens dropped", tone: dropped ? "open" : "good" };

const fmt = (v) =>
  typeof v !== "number" ? "abstained"
    : Math.abs(v) >= 1000 ? v.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 0 })
    : v.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 3 });
---

<Sheet title="Reasoning" system="03 · argue, attack, survive, weigh" sheet="03" pill={pill}>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Why there is no mesh</h2>
      <p class="sub">the lenses cannot see each other, on purpose</p>
      <p class="secondary" style="margin:0">
        Nine lenses read the same evidence and never each other's conclusions. There is no
        parameter through which one view could reach another — it is structural, not an instruction
        in a prompt. Lenses that see each other converge, converging rebuilds consensus, and
        consensus scores zero. The diversity is the asset being protected.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>What agreement is worth</h2>
      <p class="sub">less than it looks</p>
      <p class="secondary" style="margin:0">
        Agreement between lenses is <em>not</em> presented as corroboration anywhere in this system.
        Isolation prevents convergence in language; it does not prevent correlated error. They read
        overlapping documents, so five being wrong together is about as likely as one. The judge is
        told to weigh by materiality — six lenses agreeing on a weak signal lose to one carrying
        the company's own guidance with a quote.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {live.map((c) => {
    const views = c.results.lenses?.views ?? [];
    const challenges = c.results.challenge?.challenges ?? [];
    const drops = c.results.reconciliation?.dropped ?? [];
    const judge = c.results.judge ?? {};
    return (
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>{c.results.header.company} <span class="muted">· {c.ticker}</span></h2>
        <p class="sub">hub and spoke — every lens has one edge to the judge and none to each other</p>

        <div class="scroll">
          <table>
            <tr>
              <th>lens</th><th>state</th>
              {c.results.forecast.metrics.map((m) => <th class="num">{m.metric_label}</th>)}
              <th class="num">stated</th><th class="num">survived</th>
            </tr>
            {views.map((v) => {
              const ch = challenges.find((x) => x.lens === v.lens);
              const drop = drops.find((d) => d.lens === v.lens);
              const abstained = (v.estimates ?? []).every((e) => e.estimate === null);
              return (
                <tr class={drop ? "row-drop" : abstained ? "row-abstain" : ""}>
                  <td><b>{v.lens.replace("lens_", "")}</b>{v.deterministic && <span class="muted"> · no model</span>}</td>
                  <td>
                    {drop ? <span style="color:var(--critical)">dropped</span>
                      : abstained ? <span class="muted">abstained</span>
                      : <span style="color:var(--good)">counted</span>}
                  </td>
                  {c.results.forecast.metrics.map((m) => {
                    const e = (v.estimates ?? []).find((x) =>
                      (x.metric_label ?? "").toLowerCase().includes(m.metric_label.toLowerCase().split(",")[0].slice(0, 12)),
                    );
                    return <td class="num">{e ? fmt(e.estimate) : "—"}</td>;
                  })}
                  <td class="num muted">{ch?.stated_confidence ?? "—"}</td>
                  <td class="num">{ch ? <b>{ch.surviving_confidence}</b> : "—"}</td>
                </tr>
              );
            })}
          </table>
        </div>

        {drops.length > 0 && (
          <div class="dropbox">
            <b>Dropped, and why.</b> A dropped lens is dropped whole, never claim by claim — a lens
            that fabricated one citation has told you something about the rest of its reasoning.
            <ul>
              {drops.map((d) => (
                <li><b>{d.lens}</b> — {d.reason}{d.quote && <div class="quote">“{d.quote}”</div>}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        )}

        {challenges.length > 0 && (
          <details>
            <summary>argue, attack, survive — per lens</summary>
            {challenges.map((ch) => (
              <div class="chal">
                <div class="chalhead">
                  <b>{ch.lens.replace("lens_", "")}</b>
                  <span class="muted">stated {ch.stated_confidence} → survived {ch.surviving_confidence}
                    {ch.erosion > 0 && ` · eroded ${ch.erosion.toFixed(2)}`}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="grid two">
                  <div><span class="tag">argued</span><p>{ch.strongest_case}</p></div>
                  <div><span class="tag attack">attacked</span><p>{ch.strongest_attack}</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="grid two">
                  <div><span class="tag">survived</span><p>{ch.survived}</p></div>
                  <div><span class="tag">broke</span><p>{ch.broke}</p></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </details>
        )}

        <div class="judgebox">
          <b>What the judge did.</b>
          {judge.degraded && <span style="color:var(--serious)"> DEGRADED — {judge.degrade_reason}</span>}
          {(judge.metrics ?? []).map((m) => (
            <div class="jrow"><b>{m.metric_label}</b><p>{m.rationale}</p>
              <p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">weighting: {m.weighting}</p></div>
          ))}
          {judge.missing_lenses_considered && (
            <p class="muted" style="font-size:12.5px">
              <b>Absent views were named to it, not hidden:</b> {judge.missing_lenses_considered}
            </p>
          )}
        </div>
      </div>
    );
  })}
</Sheet>

<style>
  .row-drop td { opacity: .75; }
  .row-abstain td { opacity: .55; }
  .dropbox { margin-top: 14px; padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--critical); border-radius: 10px; background: #2410103d; font-size: 13px; }
  .dropbox ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  .dropbox li { margin-bottom: 7px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  details { margin-top: 14px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .chal { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 12px 0; }
  .chalhead { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 13px; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--series-3); }
  .tag.attack { color: var(--serious); }
  .chal p { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 4px 0 10px; }
  .judgebox { margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 13px; }
  .jrow { margin-top: 10px; }
  .jrow p { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 3px 0; }
</style>
